  "answer": "Based on my research, the country that meets all your criteria is **Nigeria**.\n\n**Verification:**\n\n1. **CCPI 2024 \"medium\" rating**: Nigeria ranked 17th with a score of 63.88. The CCPI website explicitly describes Nigeria as \"first among countries with medium performance\" in the 2024 index.\n\n2. **Non-EU (excluding UK)**: Nigeria is not an EU member nor the UK.\n\n3. **2023 HDI < 0.7**: Nigeria's 2023 Human Development Index value is **0.560** (ranked 164th globally), well below the 0.7 threshold.\n\n4. **2023 GDP > $350 billion**: According to World Bank World Development Indicators, Nigeria's 2023 GDP (current US$) was approximately **$363.8 billion**, exceeding the $350 billion threshold.\n\nNo other non-EU country with a CCPI 2024 \"medium\" rating simultaneously has an HDI below 0.7 and GDP above $350 billion (Pakistan has HDI 0.544 but GDP ~$340B; India has GDP ~$3.5T but CCPI rating \"high\"; Egypt, Brazil, Thailand, Vietnam, Indonesia, Mexico, South Africa all have HDI > 0.7).",
